/*****************************************************************************
    jitJUi -- THE ITERATOR-ARM PIN for rung JU. 2026-08-03.

    ⚠ THIS FIXTURE EXISTS TO PIN A GATE ORDERING, NOT TO TEST ITERATORS.

    opPlusPlus and opMinusMinus each test the iterator arm BEFORE the jitting
    gate:

        if result.fLAG      return 0;          <- poisoned iterator
        if isIterator { ... return result; }   <- THE ITERATOR ARM
        if jitting  { jitEmitUnary(...) }      <- the emit gate

    So an iterator node under ++ never reaches jitEmitUnary: it falls through
    to interpretation. That ordering is Tony's signed ruling of 2026-08-03 and
    it is SEQUENCING, not feasibility -- the arm is expected to be jittable and
    is WANTED jitted later. The gate sits where moving it INTO the iterator arm
    is a move rather than a rebuild.

    ⚠ WHY A FIXTURE AND NOT A COMMENT: nothing enforced that ordering. A future
    refactor that hoists the jitting gate above the iterator arm -- an entirely
    reasonable-looking tidy -- would route iterator nodes into jitEmitUnary,
    where they would be seeded as data fields and increment an ADDRESS. This
    fixture makes that refactor go red.

    ⚠ AND IT PINS A SECOND THING, introduced the same day. Fixing the unary
    crash widened runOP's seed gate to

        if jitting && (op.isOperator || op.isUnary)

    which means an iterator operand under ++ is now SEEDED IN runOP, upstream,
    before opPlusPlus gets the chance to take its iterator arm. That seeding is
    new, and it is exactly the kind of upstream side effect that is invisible
    until something depends on it. This fixture is the thing that depends on it.

    ============================================================================
    ⚠ WHAT IT ASSERTS -- A PINNED KNOWN DIVERGENCE, and the first draft of this
    fixture asserted the WRONG THING. Recorded because the correction is the
    finding.

    It was written to assert `jitted == interpreted`, on the reasoning that
    iterator semantics are parked with Tony so a fixed count would be pinning an
    answer this arc has no standing to choose. That premise was fine. The
    ASSERTION was not, because it assumed the two agreed today. They do not:

        JUi jitted      : juiCount = 0
        JUi interpreted : juiCount = 2

    ⚠ AND THE DIVERGENCE IS PRE-EXISTING -- MEASURED, NOT ASSUMED. The obvious
    suspect was this arc: widening runOP's seed gate to include isUnary means an
    iterator operand under ++ is now seeded upstream, which is exactly the kind
    of change that would produce this. So the gate was REVERTED to isOperator-
    only, retok'd, rebuilt, and re-run:

        pre-fix  gate (isOperator)            jitted 0 / interpreted 2
        post-fix gate (isOperator||isUnary)   jitted 0 / interpreted 2

    Identical. The unary fix did not cause it, and a jitted iterator walk
    visiting nothing is a defect that predates this arc. Not chased -- iterator
    semantics are Tony's, and `2` for a three-member trunk is in that same
    parked territory.

    So the fixture pins BOTH OBSERVED VALUES as a known divergence, the
    `tree.divergence` / `iterT1m` pattern: a deliberately pinned wrong answer,
    never a park (RULE H6 -- a pin whose answer has not been chosen is a park,
    and a park that silently starts holding is how it becomes forgotten).

    It still does its primary job. If a refactor hoists the jitting gate above
    the iterator arm, the iterator node reaches jitEmitUnary, is seeded as a
    data field, and increments an ADDRESS -- the numbers move or the run dies,
    and either way this goes red.

    ⚠ WHEN THE ITERATOR ARM IS JITTED (it is WANTED, per Tony's 2026-08-03
    ruling -- sequencing, not feasibility), THIS FIXTURE MUST BE RE-PINNED, and
    a re-pin needs a SENTENCE naming what changed, not a green diff.
    ============================================================================

    SENTINEL AT THE FOOT (standing harness rule H2).
*****************************************************************************/
Start();
include(unitTests);
include(generate);
include(utilities);

search reset stack Grokking;
search Generating UnitTests bcOPs Utilities list;

register(JitLadder);
define
    juiA;
    juiB;
    juiC;
    juiTrunk    juiA juiB juiC;
    juiCount;
    /*  Single level, NO recursion -- recursion through a jitted action is
        J-R's subject and would confound this pin with that one. The ++ here
        is on `g`, an ITERATOR, and the ++ on juiCount is on a DATA node, so
        one action exercises both arms of opPlusPlus in the same run.  */
    jitJUi code={
        juiCount = 0;
        iterate g on juiTrunk;
        while ++g
            ++juiCount;
        };
    ;

juiCount = 0;
testing(jitJUi);
print "JUi jitted      : juiCount =" juiCount:;

/*  The oracle, captured LAST -- calling the action interpreted BEFORE
    testing() consumes its isCoded state (measured on J3, 2026-07-31).  */
juiCount = 0;
jitJUi();
print "JUi interpreted : juiCount =" juiCount:;

print "JUi SENTINEL -- run reached the end":;
stop();
